    "content": "Tiger Woods has won 15 professional major championships, ranking second all-time behind Jack Nicklaus. His victories span from the 1997 Masters to the 2019 Masters, including five Masters, four PGA Championships, three U.S. Opens, and three Open Championships. Notably, he achieved the \"Tiger Slam\" in 2000-2001, holding all four major titles simultaneously.All 15 Major Championship Wins1997: Masters Tournament1999: PGA Championship2000: U.S. Open, Open Championship, PGA Championship2001: Masters Tournament2002: Masters Tournament, U.S. Open2005: Masters Tournament, Open Championship2006: Open Championship, PGA Championship2007: PGA Championship2008: U.S. Open2019: Masters TournamentKey Major Records and HighlightsSecond All-Time: Trails only Jack Nicklaus (18) in total professional major wins.The Tiger Slam: In 2000-2001, he became the only player to win four consecutive professional majors (2000 U.S. Open, 2000 Open, 2000 PGA, 2001 Masters).Youngest Masters Winner: Won his first Masters in 1997 at age 21.Largest Margin: His 1997 Masters win was by a record 12 strokes.Final Round Lead: Woods is 14–1 in majors when holding at least a share of the lead going into the final round.",
